Reject codebooks with a value mapping (lookup type 1 or 2) and zero dimensions.

vorbis_decbook_unpack() reads the 16-bit dimension field into a signed char, so e.g. 0x0200
becomes 0, and the ov_ilog() size check passes. For lookup type 1 it skips
_book_maptype1_quantvals() when dim == 0, but vorbis_book_init_decode() later calls
_book_unquantize(), which calls _book_maptype1_quantvals(0, entries) unguarded: pow(entries,
1/0.f) is inf, and the search loop never satisfies its exit test with dim == 0 (vals is
incremented forever). Decoding hangs in vorbis_synthesis_init(). Reject such books at unpack
time instead; books without a value mapping keep dim 0 working.
This also covers residue stage books: res0_unpack() requires a value mapping for them, so a
stage book can no longer have dim 0, and vorbis_book_decodevs_add() (residue type 0) can no
longer divide n by a zero book->dim on the first audio packet.
Includes test/test_codebook_zero_dim.c.
Upstream: open MR xiph/vorbis!51 (by gruenich, 2026-11-06; fixes #2363) rejects dim < 1 only
for books referenced by a residue (in res0_unpack()), which fixes the decodevs_add division
but does not cover a book that only exists in the codebook list; not fixed as of 1b75110b
(master HEAD on 2026-11-21).

diff --git a/lib/codebook.c b/lib/codebook.c
index 2945af80..a25c4505 100644
--- a/lib/codebook.c
+++ b/lib/codebook.c
@@ -235,6 +235,9 @@ int vorbis_decbook_unpack(dec_codebook *c,oggpack_buffer *opb){
   case 1: case 2:
     /* implicitly populated value mapping */
     /* explicitly populated value mapping */
+    /* a value mapping needs at least one dimension: with dim 0,
+       _book_maptype1_quantvals() never terminates */
+    if(c->dim<1)goto _eofout;
 
     c->q_min=(ogg_uint32_t)oggpack_read(opb,32);
     c->q_delta=(ogg_uint32_t)oggpack_read(opb,32);
@@ -247,7 +250,7 @@ int vorbis_decbook_unpack(dec_codebook *c,oggpack_buffer *opb){
       int quantvals=0;
       switch(c->maptype){
       case 1:
-        quantvals=(c->dim==0?0:_book_maptype1_quantvals(c->dim, c->entries));
+        quantvals=_book_maptype1_quantvals(c->dim, c->entries);
         break;
       case 2:
         quantvals=c->entries*c->dim;
